direction: down
start: Start here\nParse and validate source gates {
  style: {fill: "#19354D"; font-color: white; bold: true}
}
valid: Inputs and destination valid? {shape: diamond}
planned: Planned — exit 0\nComplete order without temporary file
temp: Stage private .bookscan-prepare-*.tmp\nExclusive 0600 file saved through stream
check: Copy adapter reopens and compares graphs\nAll geometry, markers and declarations
ready: Recheck sources and set final mode\nFlush and fsync complete file
publish: Defer INT / TERM across no-clobber link\nRecord committed before restoring signals
success: Written — exit 0\nComplete PDF with temporary name removed
warning: Written — exit 0 with warnings\nSignal, cleanup or stdout failure
failure: Report actionable error\nNo new destination before commit
start -> valid: 1. Resolve order and destination aliases
valid -> planned: 2a. Dry-run after source recheck
valid -> temp: 2b. Write
valid -> failure: Invalid input or source recheck fails
temp -> check: 3. Copy succeeds
temp -> failure: Write error or cancellation
check -> ready: 4. Validation succeeds
check -> failure: Validation error or cancellation
ready -> publish: 5. Ready to commit
ready -> failure: Source change, I/O or cancellation
publish -> success: 6. Link succeeds = commit point
publish -> failure: Destination exists or link fails
success -> warning: 7. Post-commit reporting / cleanup
